-- title:
--   Dual cotype bounds from L2 moment lifts
-- statement:
--   A normed space $Z$ satisfies the fixed cotype bound of length $m$ with constant $D$ if $\bigl(\sum_{i\le m}\|z_i\|^2\bigr)^{1/2}\le D\bigl(\mathbb E\|\sum_{i\le m}\varepsilon_iz_i\|^2\bigr)^{1/2}$ for all $z_1,\dots,z_m\in Z$. Let $X$ be a real normed space and $C\ge0$. Suppose every $z_1,\dots,z_m\in X$ admit $H:\{0,1\}^m\to X$ with moments $\mathbb E_u\varepsilon_i(u)H(u)=z_i$ and
--   $$
--   \bigl(\mathbb E\|H\|^2\bigr)^{1/2}\le C\Bigl(\sum_i\|z_i\|^2\Bigr)^{1/2}.
--   $$
--   Then $X^*$ satisfies the fixed cotype bound of length $m$ with constant $C$.
--
--   Lifting moments with control is dual to the cotype inequality.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/DualCotypeFromLifts.lean#L11-L29

